Crowds are filling Cleveland Public Auditorium Saturday afternoon as attendees await former President Barack Obama’s appearance, his first visit to Ohio since 2018.

Obama last came to Cleveland to campaign for Democratic gubernatorial candidate Richard Cordray. This time, he’s returning to support Amy Acton for governor and Sherrod Brown for U.S. Senate, with Election Day set for Tuesday, Nov. 3.

// 📹➡️ @joshduke.cle, clevelanddotcom // #BarackObama #ClevelandOhio #OhioPolitics #Election2026 #SherrodBrown

